---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { siteContent } from '../../data/siteContent';

const note = siteContent.notes[0];

const noteArticleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: `${note.title}: ${note.subtitle}`,
  description: note.summary,
  datePublished: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: siteContent.meta.name, url: siteContent.meta.url },
  keywords: note.tags.join(', '),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={`${note.title} — ${siteContent.meta.name}`} description={note.summary} canonicalPath="/notes/flexible-but-not-free">
  <main id="main-content" class="wrap pt-12 sm:pt-20 pb-28 sm:pb-40">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">

      <!-- Back Link -->
      <div>
        <a href="/#writing" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">
          <span>←</span>
          <span>Back to Home &amp; Writing</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Header -->
      <header class="tactile-card p-8 sm:p-12 space-y-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs font-mono text-[var(--muted)]">
          <span class="text-[var(--accent)] font-semibold">{note.category}</span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>{note.date}</span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>{note.readTime}</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)] leading-[1.15]">
          {note.title}
        </h1>

        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-[var(--ink-2)] leading-relaxed">
          {note.subtitle}
        </p>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-[var(--line)] flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {note.tags.map((t) => (
            <span class="tech-pill font-mono">{t}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Article Content -->
      <article class="tactile-card p-8 sm:p-14 text-base sm:text-lg leading-[1.8] text-[var(--ink-2)] space-y-8">
        <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl leading-[1.5] text-[var(--ink)] font-heading font-medium">
          Every gig platform promises the same bargain: work whenever you want, earn on your own schedule, keep complete
          freedom over your week. When you're studying full-time in a city as expensive as Toronto, that pitch sounds like
          the perfect arrangement.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have a networking lab at George Brown on Monday morning, a routing assignment due Tuesday night and an exam
          on Friday, traditional shift work is hard to fit around classes. App-based work seems to solve that by letting you
          log on whenever there's a gap.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time, though, you notice the flexibility isn't actually free. The cost just shows up somewhere else — in
          fragmented attention, physical wear, and the slow erosion of deep study time.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)] pt-6">Three hours aren't three hours</h2>
        <p>
          On paper, three separate one-hour gaps look the same as one three-hour block. In practice they aren't close.
          Studying subnetting, fixing a broken Linux DHCP config or building a multi-VM Active Directory lab needs
          uninterrupted focus just to load the problem into your head.
        </p>
        <p>
          When the day is split between traffic, notifications and short shifts, you never really get there. Even after you
          sit back down, it takes a while before you're thinking clearly again.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)] pt-6">The costs you don't see on payday</h2>
        <p>
          The financial math is equally deceptive. What shows up in your bank account is gross revenue, not net income.
          Between commercial insurance considerations, frequent brake pad wear, Toronto winter pothole damage, and accelerating vehicle depreciation,
          the real hourly margin is significantly thinner than the dashboard implies.
        </p>
        <p>
          More critically, the opportunity cost compound over time. An hour spent driving delivery is an hour not spent troubleshooting
          OSPF neighbor adjacencies, writing automation scripts, or building systems that create lasting career leverage.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)] pt-6">Reframing the tradeoff</h2>
        <p>
          Gig platforms can serve as an emergency safety valve, but treating them as a sustainable operating model while pursuing an intensive
          systems curriculum creates chronic cognitive debt. Recognizing that friction early is what pushed me to guard my calendar,
          treat lab time as non-negotiable, and focus relentlessly on acquiring technical depth.
        </p>

        <div class="pt-8 border-t border-[var(--line)] flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono text-[var(--muted)]">
          <span>Written by Tarik Gungor · Toronto, ON</span>
          <a href="/#writing" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">← Back to Home</a>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(noteArticleSchema)} />
</BaseLayout>
